# %% markdown cell 1b4dea1526009357
+# Flat AB performance comparison
+
+The technical source is a centered **AB 20 flat $f_\nu$ continuum**. All configurations use the same evaluated atmospheric transmission, continuum and PALACE airglow, with dark sky, airmass 1.1, seeing 0.65 arcsec and MJD 60310.25.
+
+Both X-shooter modes are executed: faint continuum (1.0/0.9/0.9 arcsec, spectral CCD binning by two) and higher resolution (0.8/0.9/0.6 arcsec, unbinned). ZShooter is evaluated with natural seeing and a 0.70 arcsec slit, AO and a 0.33 arcsec slit, and a natural-seeing 0.33 arcsec control. Its selected Zemax prescription and explicit detector offsets are used unchanged.
+
+Native detector pixels are extracted with transparent boxcars. Optical rates are reused for explicit exposure scenarios within each unchanged detector package. The figures distinguish instrumental throughput, extracted fraction, geometric slit resolution, simulated point-source resolution, and sensitivity with or without OH sample selection.
+
